1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,060
How much should you put in one trade?

2
00:00:02,602 --> 00:00:03,927
Here's the simple maths.

3
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:07,463
Start with your account, say one thousand MB.

4
00:00:07,812 --> 00:00:17,786
Decide to risk one percent, so ten MB. If your stop is five percent away, your position is two hundred MB, because five percent of two hundred is ten.

5
00:00:18,286 --> 00:00:22,893
That way, even ten losses in a row leave you with about ninety percent of your account.

6
00:00:23,301 --> 00:00:24,951
No single trade can sink you.

7
00:00:25,786 --> 00:00:29,277
Practise sizing with practice money at memestreet.net.

